# Module architecture

Maven layout is documented in `docs/project-structure.md`. Follow it when adding code or modules.

- `app` — `@SpringBootApplication`, properties, Flyway, Actuator. No feature controllers or entities.
- `shared` — Lombok, Validation, Web MVC. HTTP envelope and prefixes: `api/` (`AppApi`, `WebApi`, `ApiPaths`), later `exception/` (`GlobalExceptionHandler`, `ResourceNotFoundException`), `response/` (`ApiResponse`, `ErrorResponse`), `pagination/` (`PageResponse`), `validation/`. Do not implement those extra classes until a feature needs them. No feature controllers, entities, Spring Security, Redis, or JPA infrastructure.
- `core` — depends on `shared`; Data JPA. Infrastructure: `persistence/` (`BaseEntity`, `AuditableEntity`, `JpaConfig`), later `cache/RedisConfig`, `messaging/KafkaConfig` only if we use Kafka, and `config/`. Domain security types live in `security/` (`Role`, `Permission`, `RolePermissions`) — no `GrantedAuthority`, no Spring Security dependency. No controllers or feature entities. Redis/Kafka starters go on `core` when those packages are added — not on a feature.

- `features/<name>` — one jar per feature: `auth`, `user`, `movie`, `theatre`, `show`, `booking`, `payment`, `review`.
- Each feature depends on `core` only. Features do not depend on each other.
- `app` depends on every feature. Security reaches the process through `features/auth`.
- Spring Security starter and `SecurityFilterChain` / JWT filters belong in `features/auth`, never in `core` or `shared`.
- Screen/Seat live in `theatre`. BookingSeat lives in `booking`.
- Do not add `api`/`domain`/`data` as extra Maven modules unless a feature is large enough to need it (see the docs). Until then those are **packages** inside the feature jar.
